# QA Automation Pipeline — Quality Gates

## Row validation statuses

`Valid` | `Valid with warnings` | `Invalid` | `Requires clarification`

Invalid → no generation.

## Gate A — Generation

- Excel row valid (or valid with warnings)
- Traceable test-case ID
- Steps and expected results sufficiently clear
- Automation feasibility confirmed
- Assumptions documented
- Framework identified (Playwright + TS POM)
- Every eligible UI case has evidence from the live module route, controls/actions, and expected-result target
- `liveUiValidatedCaseIds` exactly covers eligible UI case IDs and `liveUiCoveragePercent=100`
- Every generated/reused locator is validated against the current live DOM
- Figma, Excel, mocks, and heal shells do not count as live-UI evidence

## Gate B — Execution

- Syntax OK; project conventions followed
- Meaningful assertions; no hard-coded credentials
- Traceability to source TC ID
- Exactly six deterministic near-equal batches cover every eligible ID once
- Each non-empty batch has one evidence-backed pre-heal Playwright run
- Only classified automation failures enter healing
- At most one healer invocation and one changed-case verification run per batch
- Pre-heal and post-heal Passed / Failed / Blocked counts are evidence-backed

## Gate C — Final

- Executed successfully **or** blocked with documented external reason
- Every eligible UI case passed the 100% live-generation evidence gate
- All six batches completed and aggregate counts equal the batch totals
- Remaining failures after the permitted batch heal cycle are classified and preserved
- Risks documented; final report complete
- Run checkpoint `results/qa-pipeline/final/state.json` ends at `currentStage=done` / `status=done` (or `blocked` with reason)
- If an agent died mid-run: auto-resume from checkpoint — do not leave Gate C pending for user “continue”

## Case states

Received → Input validated → Invalid | Normalized → Batch assigned → Live UI validated | Generation blocked → Generated → Batch executed → Healing eligible | Healed and verified | Final | Requires clarification

Record timestamp, result, evidence, reason on each transition.
